%% C4 Dynamic diagram: the office fire, times as measured in Section 11
sequenceDiagram
  participant SRC as Fire and physics
  participant SEN as Sensors
  participant INT as Detector and agent
  participant ACT as Safety rules and actions
  participant EVA as Evacuation
  participant BS as BuildSim
  rect rgb(254, 243, 226)
    SRC->>SEN: 1: fire starts at t=0.<br/>Smoke, CO and heat rise
    SEN->>INT: 2: a reading every 5 s,<br/>delayed, noisy, capped
    Note over INT: 3: t=51 s, P reaches 0.35: INVESTIGATING
    Note over INT: 4: t=81 s, P above 0.55 for 20 s: PRE-ALARM
    Note over INT: 5: t=106 s, 25 s in pre-alarm, P=0.91: CONFIRMED
  end
  rect rgb(254, 226, 226)
    INT->>ACT: 6: sprinkler on, door closed,<br/>evacuate, each with a reason
    ACT->>SRC: 7: allowed: 331 °C backs up the smoke, the room is empty.<br/>Sprinkler on, door 0.15 open
  end
  rect rgb(220, 242, 228)
    ACT->>EVA: 8: everyone starts to leave
    EVA->>BS: 9: route out of the fire room,<br/>41 nodes down to exit A1016
    SRC->>SEN: 10: next step, heat x0.25<br/>and smoke x0.4. The readings bend
    SRC->>BS: 11: once a simulated second: heat maps,<br/>effects, alerts, doors, people
    EVA->>BS: 12: t=217 s, last person out.<br/>RSET recorded
  end
